From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Longwei Yang <19267252+Longwei-Yang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:36:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Safarium: customizable sidebar toolbar, panel polish,
 restore fix

Vertical tabs:
- Sidebar toolbar with its own layout (NSUserDefaults
  SafariumSidebarToolbarLayout): adjacent items share a Liquid Glass
  group, a space starts a new group, a flexible space takes the row's
  leftover width, and a row break starts a new row. Right-click >
  Customize Toolbar... edits it in place with an NSPopover palette.
- The sidebar is resizable from its trailing edge (240-480 pt, saved),
  opaque like the toolbar, with a system separator line.
- In full screen the first row takes the traffic lights' room.

Extension side panels dock on the right only, open and close with
Chrome's side panel motion (350 ms), and use the system separator color.

Tab Overview always scrolls the current card into view. The active tab
is made visible when a restored window first shows (the page stayed
blank until a tab switch). Settings and the New Tab page no longer link
to Chromium's own toolbar customization.

Default layouts: [back forward] [reload] ... [new tab, downloads,
share, overview] horizontally; [back forward] [new tab, reload] /
[overview, share, downloads] in the sidebar.

Local checkpoint only; not intended for upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
